{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f3a9c210-9000-4a00-b000-auth-nodejs",
    "name": "Nodejs API",
    "description": "## Auth API (`/auth/*`)\n\n### Email delivery\nOTP, password-reset, and welcome emails are sent via SMTP (Hostinger/Titan). Configure **`EMAIL_*`**, **`APP_NAME`** (Property 973), and **`APP_PUBLIC_URL`** in `config.env`. Set **`OTP_HIDE_FROM_RESPONSE=1`** in production.\n\n**Branded templates:** OTP emails show the code in a Property 973–styled layout with a **Copy code** button. Password-reset emails include a **Reset password** CTA. Welcome emails use the same theme after OTP verify.\n\n**OTP copy helper:** **GET `/auth/otp/copy?code=`** — opened from the email **Copy code** button; returns HTML that auto-copies the code. Uses **`APP_API_PUBLIC_URL`** when set, otherwise **`APP_PUBLIC_URL`** (must reach this API).\n\n### Register\n- **POST `/auth/register`** — `{ \"fullName\", \"mobileNumber\", \"email\", \"password\" }`; branded OTP emailed to **`email`**.\n\n### OTP login\n- **POST `/auth/otp/send`** → **POST `/auth/otp/verify`** — OTP emailed to the account email (user must be **`mobile_verified`**).\n\n### Password reset\n**Option A — reset link (branded email):**\n- **POST `/auth/forgot-password`** — `{ \"email\" }`.\n- **GET `/auth/reset-password/verify?resetToken=`** · **POST `/auth/reset-password`**.\n\n**Option B — mobile + OTP (OTP emailed):**\n- **POST `/auth/forgot-password`** — `{ \"mobileNumber\" }`.\n- **POST `/auth/forgot-password/verify-otp`** — `{ \"mobileNumber\", \"otp\" }` → **`data.resetToken`**.\n- **POST `/auth/reset-password`**.\n\nDev: **`PASSWORD_RESET_RETURN_TOKEN_IN_RESPONSE=1`** → email forgot-password may return **`data.resetToken`**.\n\n### Users API (`/api/users`)\n- **GET `/api/users`** — Bearer JWT; paginated list.\n- **PATCH `/api/users/:id`** — Bearer JWT; update own profile only.\n\n### Before you send requests\n1. Import **Local.postman_environment.json** and select **Local · Nodejs Auth**.\n2. Set **`sampleEmail`** to an inbox you can read (or rely on **`data.otp`** in dev).\n3. Run **`npm run db:migrate`**.\n\n### Flow · new user\n1. **Register** (with email) → check inbox for branded OTP (or use **`data.otp`** / **GET OTP copy page**).\n2. **OTP Verify** → tokens + welcome email.\n\n### Collection variables\n`lastOtp`, `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, `userId`, `resetToken`, `countryId`, `stateId`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "version": "2.5.0"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "lastOtp", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "countryId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "stateId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "resetToken", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Signup · OTP verify",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "try {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.test(\"success true\", () => pm.expect(j).to.have.property('success', true));",
                  "  if (j.data?.otp !== undefined && j.data.otp !== '') {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('lastOtp', String(j.data.otp));",
                  "    pm.test(\"data.otp present\", () => pm.expect(j.data.otp).to.match(/^\\d{6}$/));",
                  "  } else if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    console.warn('Register: no data.otp (server may have OTP_HIDE_FROM_RESPONSE=1).');",
                  "  }",
                  "} catch (e) { pm.test(\"Valid JSON\", () => { throw e; }); }"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"fullName\": \"{{sampleFullName}}\",\n  \"mobileNumber\": \"{{sampleMobile}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{sampleEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{samplePassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
            "description": "**POST `/auth/register`**\nCreates user with `mobile_verified: false`. **`email`** is required; a branded Property 973 OTP email is sent (code + **Copy code** button).\nReturns `data.mobileNumber`, `data.email`, `data.emailMasked`, `data.expiresInSeconds`, and usually **`data.otp`** unless `OTP_HIDE_FROM_RESPONSE=1`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST OTP Verify",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const otp = pm.collectionVariables.get('lastOtp');",
                  "if (!otp || otp.length !== 6) {",
                  "  console.warn('lastOtp is missing or invalid — run Register or OTP Send first, or paste a 6-digit code in body.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "try {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (pm.response.code === 200 && j.success && j.data) {",
                  "    if (j.data.accessToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', j.data.accessToken);",
                  "    if (j.data.refreshToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', j.data.refreshToken);",
                  "    pm.test(\"Tokens captured\", () => pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')).to.be.ok);",
                  "  }",
                  "} catch (_e) { console.warn('OTP Verify: could not parse JSON'); }"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"mobileNumber\": \"{{sampleMobile}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{lastOtp}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify",
            "description": "**POST `/auth/otp/verify`**\nBody: `mobileNumber`, `otp` (use **`{{lastOtp}}`** from Register or OTP Send). Returns `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, `user`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
